Ordinance must fully comply with 49 C.F.R. Part 571.500 (Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standards for Low-Speed Vehicles), as may be amended from time to time. At a minimum, each LSV must be factory-equipped with:

- (a) Seatbelts for all designated seating positions;

- (b) A windshield meeting applicable safety standards;

- (c) Front and rear DOT-compliant lighting systems, including headlamps, taillamps, stop lamps, and turn signal lamps;

- (d) A parking brake; and

- (e) A vehicle identification number (VIN).

LSVs must maintain all federally required equipment in proper working order at all times.

Removal or disabling of any required equipment shall render the LSV ineligible for operation under this Ordinance.

